          Incoming interface: vlan30
          Outgoing interface list: vlan1, vlan20
      show hsl fib (hardware):
        Group (ff1e::1:100) Source (fd32:b1f0:dff8:d703::1)  L2 L3 Entry, Mirror To CPU: No
          L3 IIf = 330; L3 outgoing 301 (vlan1), 320 (vlan20)
        IPv6 (S,G) Forwarding Entries: 1

NOTES
  - vlan1's reporter is IE520-sa itself: the SA's MLD snooping (report suppression on)
    proxied eth2's join up its router port (sa3), as a snooping switch should.
  - `service pim6` is REQUIRED first: without it `ipv6 multicast-routing` answers
    "% PIM-SMv6 protocol daemon is not running or feature license is not available".
  - `show platform table ipmulti` exists but lists only an "IPv4 Multicast Route Table"
    (per member: the 224.0.0.0/24 link entry) -- no IPv6 section at all, even with the
    (S,G) above installed. The IPv6 hardware entry is visible in `show hsl fib` instead.
